environment.description:
[ENVIRONMENT INFO:
Name: SUCC campus (Supernatural University of Central California);
Domain: Collegiate Supernatural Sanctuary & Academic Domain;
Coordinates & Span: 129 Hocus Way, coastal Solarton, California;
Setting & Metaphysics: Historic premier higher-education campus founded in 1887; balanced human-supernatural integration;
Dominant Presence: University Board of Regents, Student Body (8,000 students, 60/40 supernatural/human), Greek Row (10 houses), Faculty, DCC Fellows]

[LORE & ENVIRONMENT:
Atmosphere & Senses: Salty sea breeze mingled with coffee from The Roasted Bean, old parchment, ozone from arcane labs, freshly cut athletic turf;
Spatial Architecture: Collegiate gothic stone halls, arched cloisters, modern bioengineering glass cubes, Greek Row mansions, St. Neptune athletic complex;
Rifts & Dimensional Drift: Heavily anchored runic boundary wards preventing unauthorized dimensional tears on campus grounds;
Hazards & Rules: Strict scent suppressor compliance in lecture halls, mandatory neutral truce across rival houses and packs, no lethal dueling]

[CONTEXT & SECRETS:
Cosmology & Origins: Established to foster peaceful co-existence and academic mastery between supernatural lineages and mortals;
Secrets: The subterranean Basilica library basement (Room 005) hides forgotten pre-treaty pact archives and covert summoning circles]

location.description:
[LOCATION INFO:
Era: 2024 (Modern Fantasy / Post-Gate Era);
Location: Greenhouse (Botanical Annex, Science Quarter, SUCC);
Setting: Expansive multi-story glass conservatory cultivating rare magical herbs, carnivorous plants, and medicinal flora;
Factions: Department of Herbalism & Botany, Campus Potion Brewers, Demihuman Naturalists;
Conflicts: Preventing invasive carnivorous plants from biting student gardeners, maintaining delicate tropical microclimates;
Society: Nurturing botanical dedication, peaceful natural contemplation, organic herbal alchemy]

[LORE & ENVIRONMENT:
Environment: Dense humid tropical air, rich loamy potting soil, fragrance of night-blooming orchids, sweet nectar, and mist;
Architecture: Victorian-inspired iron and tempered glass dome, multi-tier plant terraces, automated misting systems, koi ponds;
Security & Wards: Reinforced safety glass, specialized warning signs around poisonous and carnivorous plant enclosures;
Demographics: Botany majors, herbology researchers, dryads, fae students feeling at home among green leaves;
Rules & Restrictions: Do not touch labeled toxic specimens, wipe potting dirt off shoes before leaving through the atrium]

[CONTEXT & SECRETS:
History: Maintained since the university's founding, serving as the live living repository for rare California flora;
Secrets: The locked central conservatory holds a rare specimen of the Silver Moon Fern whose spores glow during lunar eclipses]
